{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 20, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3.5-122b-a10b", "content": "My recent trip to Japan was a seamless blend of ancient tradition and futuristic innovation. Beginning in Tokyo, I was immediately struck by the electric energy of Shibuya Crossing, where thousands of people flowed in perfect rhythm. Yet, just steps away, the serene atmosphere of the Meiji Shrine offered a moment of profound peace, with towering cedar trees blocking out the city noise.\n\nThe culinary journey was equally unforgettable. From a bustling street food stall in Osaka's Dotonbori district, where I devoured fresh takoyaki, to a quiet, multi-course kaiseki dinner in Kyoto, every meal felt like an art form. The attention to detail in even the simplest dish was remarkable.\n\nKyoto itself is a time capsule. Wandering through the vermilion torii gates of Fushimi Inari Taisha at sunrise, the mists clinging to the path created an ethereal scene. Later, sitting in a traditional tea house, watching the graceful tea ceremony, I felt a deep connection to centuries of culture preserved with meticulous care.\n\nThe Shinkansen, or bullet train, bridged these worlds with incredible speed, whisking me from the neon lights of the capital to the quiet temples of the countryside in under two and a half hours. The efficiency and politeness of the Japanese people made every interaction pleasant and memorable.\n\nThis journey was more than just sightseeing; it was an immersion into a unique way of life. Japan's ability to honor its past while embracing the future is truly inspiring. I left with a full heart, a camera full of photos, and a strong desire to return soon. If you ever get the chance, pack your bags and experience the magic of Japan for yourself.", "logprobs": [{"token": "My", "logprob": -2.0766354}, {"token": " recent", "logprob": -0.060799994}, {"token": " trip", "logprob": -0.7884185}, {"token": " to", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -4.